
            The Windows Explorer Context Menu plugin for FAR
                   Version 1.5, 12/10/99

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
DISTRIBUTION: Freeware.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This plugin allows you to invoke part of Windows Explorer context menu for the
file/directory highlighted in the FAR panel. Windows Explorer context menu
is the menu you've got when right mouse button is clicked. This way you can
keep using your favorite Explorer extensions while enjoying working with FAR.

Software was written and tested on WinNT 4.0 with FAR 1.63. It was adopted,
localized and tested on Win98 (Russian version) with FAR 1.63 by Ivan Sintyurin
(spinoza@mail.ru)

Known problems:

  In "Properties" dialog some controls have wrong color.
  Under non-English Win98 sometimes creates subdirectory with the strange
  name in the Windows directory

What's new:

1.5:
  Fixed strange behavior when after plugin was loaded starting other programs
  require a lot of time (or exit from FAR). Example: ICQ invoked from context
  menu (through plugin) hangs until FAR is closed.

1.4:
  More internationalization - now correctly works under non-english Win98
  Added configuration dialog allowing to show message after command execution
  Some online help added

1.3:
  Fixed nasty memory overrun

1.2:

  Added submenus support
  Added "Properties" dialog support

1.1:

  Fixed various problems with NLS support

1.0:

  Initial release

